  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-git-lfs-2026-105802",
  "summary": "Git LFS may execute arbitrary commands via crafted Git configurations",
  "details": "Git LFS is a Git extension for versioning large files. From 0.6.0 until 3.8.1, Git LFS reads Git configuration options defined for a submodule without checking certain values for embedded line-ending control characters. A malicious repository can insert control characters such as line feed (LF) into those values to mimic options that cause Git LFS to execute an attacker-controlled command or binary while fetching or adding objects. This issue is fixed in version 3.8.1.",
